  "observations": [
    "A real TLS held-reply regression first fails because no phase timings exist. With instrumentation it distinguishes nine queued frames from one in-flight exchange, then ten frame dequeues from three completed exchange windows.",
    "Existing lost/reordered reply, route revocation and bounded-deadline cases verify failed windows without converting prior observed admissions into failures or unknown frames into success. Joined cancellation verifies three queued abandonments, retained physical permits and one failed in-flight window.",
    "The native query/replication fixture requires actual successful queue, exchange and admission observations on both control and data lanes. The authenticated one-versus-32-group metrics fixture requires exactly 23 operations, 20 counters and 551 Prometheus sample identities.",
    "The analyzer requires the complete fixed vocabulary and retains started/completed/outcome/histogram bounds; old evidence must use its pinned analyzer. Missing new operations are not zero-filled."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No new physical benchmark or causal attribution of the earlier density burst. The next unchanged workload comparison must correlate these boundaries with queue depths and CPU observations.",
    "Exchange samples count windows, not frames or commands, and include connection/TLS setup when needed. Runtime admission does not establish Raft persistence or business acknowledgement. Different aggregate quantiles cannot be subtracted into a per-command breakdown.",
    "Instrumentation overhead, steady-state latency, equivalent-contract comparison, sustained S3 and Q1 capacity remain open. Native and Python checks do not qualify capacity or MR-14 completion.",
    "The separate cellar-multi-raft profile remains stopped; no other Colima profile was controlled."
  ],
